# Promoted from the learning loop (2026-09-19), reviewed and kept: a hardcoded
# secret baked into a Dockerfile/compose ENV assignment. Generalises over the
# ENV KEY="value" form. Scoped to container/IaC files to avoid firing on
# unrelated ENV-like text.
id: KEUR-IAC-001
ilities: [integrity]
maturity: 2
title: Hardcoded secret in a container ENV assignment
category: iac
severity: critical
engine: pattern
skip_comments: true
target:
  extensions: .env .yml .yaml
  filenames: Dockerfile
patterns:
  - regex: (?i)\bENV\s+[A-Z0-9_]*(?:PASS|PASSWORD|SECRET|TOKEN|KEY|CRED)[A-Z0-9_]*\s*=?\s*["']?([^"'\s]{6,})
    message: "Hardcoded secret in a container ENV instruction (CWE-798). Inject secrets at runtime (build args, secret mounts, or an orchestrator secret), never bake them into the image."
confidence: 0.9
fix: "Remove the literal from the Dockerfile. Provide the secret at runtime via --env-file, a secret mount, or the orchestrator's secret store. Rotate the value if it was committed."
